## Rule of the Court (Indemnity-basis costs review — DIFC common-law line)
##
## Source: indemnity-basis costs assessment as applied by the DIFC Courts,
## following the English common-law line. The governing distinction is
## stated by Cooke J. at §2 of the Schedule of Reasons in:
##
##   ENF 271/2025 — Timothy Hugh Christian Taylor v Arlette Joelle Marie
##   Madeleine Yao Affi
##   Order with Reasons of H.E. Justice Sir Jeremy Cooke, 1 April 2026.
##
##   "Where costs are ordered on the indemnity basis, there is no room
##    for arguments of proportionality – only of reasonableness of the
##    costs incurred."
##
## In contrast to standard-basis review (Trace #1) and to deadline /
## interest accrual (Trace #2), indemnity-basis review is the canonical
## case for *bounded discretion*: the rule strips one filter (proportion-
## ality) and leaves a single one (reasonableness). The reasonableness
## judgment is not a formula. The protocol's job is therefore *not* to
## compute a single award figure. It is to:
##
##   (a) dispose of structurally-defective objections automatically,
##   (b) hold rule-compliant findings deterministically, and
##   (c) bound the residual region where human judgment is required.
##
## Concretely, on the facts of ENF 271/2025:
##
##   - Defendant's objection 1: "claimant did the work himself, so
##       Hadef & Partners' bill must include time he did not pay them
##       for" — non-specific, no element of the schedule named.
##       Cooke J., §3-4: rejected as another allegation that should not
##       have been made; the protocol disposes of this category by
##       structural test (no named line item, no factual finding sought).
##
##   - Defendant's objection 2: "two lawyers were charged for hearing
##       attendance when only one attended" — specific, named, fact-
##       checkable. Cooke J., §3: rejected on evidence (both attended
##       online). The protocol holds this finding deterministically.
##
##   - Court's own residual concern, §5: "some excess in the overall
##       time spent by the senior associate" — a general qualitative
##       observation arising from the Court's examination of the
##       Schedule of Costs, not a named line item. This is the
##       irreducible discretion residue. The protocol surfaces the
##       category but cannot quantify the deduction.
##
## The award reduces the claim AED 128,914.80 → AED 120,000, a delta of
## AED 8,914.80 (≈6.92% of claim). The protocol mechanically disposes
## of objections 1 and 2; the AED 8,914.80 is the structured-discretion
## residue.
##
## Catala 1.1.0 notes:
##   - `text` fields replaced by enumerations.
##   - List comprehension `[x for o among lst if cond]` replaced with
##     `map each o among lst such that cond to x`.
##   - `exists o among lst such that cond` replaced with
##     `(number of (list of o among lst such that cond)) > 0`.

```catala
declaration enumeration ObjectionId:
  -- ClaimantDidWorkHimself
  -- DoubleCounselChargedForHearing
  -- ExcessSeniorAssociateTime

declaration enumeration FactualFinding:
  -- Rejected_Unspecific
  -- Rejected_On_Evidence
  -- Accepted_With_Named_Amount
  -- Requires_Human_Judgment

declaration structure Objection:
  data objection content ObjectionId
  data names_specific_line_item content boolean
  data factual_finding content FactualFinding
  data named_amount_aed content decimal

declaration structure Schedule:
  data claimed_aed content decimal
  data objections content list of Objection

declaration structure ReviewOutcome:
  data mechanically_disposed_aed content decimal
  data deterministic_reductions_aed content decimal
  data residual_discretion_lower_aed content decimal
  data residual_discretion_upper_aed content decimal
  data requires_human_judgment content boolean

declaration scope IndemnityBasisReview:
  input schedule content Schedule
  output review content ReviewOutcome

scope IndemnityBasisReview:
  ## Indemnity basis: only reasonableness, no proportionality.
  ## Rule encoded:
  ##   1. An objection that does not name a specific element of the
  ##      schedule is mechanically disposed (Cooke J., §4).
  ##   2. An objection that names a line item AND has a factual finding
  ##      Rejected_On_Evidence contributes 0 to the reduction.
  ##   3. An objection that names a line item AND has a factual finding
  ##      Accepted_With_Named_Amount contributes its named amount.
  ##   4. Any other category is bounded discretion: the protocol cannot
  ##      derive the reduction.
  definition review equals
    let det_reductions equals
      sum decimal of (map each o among schedule.objections
                      such that (o.names_specific_line_item
                                 and (match o.factual_finding with pattern
                                      -- Accepted_With_Named_Amount: true
                                      -- Rejected_Unspecific: false
                                      -- Rejected_On_Evidence: false
                                      -- Requires_Human_Judgment: false))
                      to o.named_amount_aed)
    in
    let residual_count equals
      number of (list of o among schedule.objections
                 such that ((not o.names_specific_line_item)
                            or (match o.factual_finding with pattern
                                -- Requires_Human_Judgment: true
                                -- Rejected_Unspecific: false
                                -- Rejected_On_Evidence: false
                                -- Accepted_With_Named_Amount: false)))
    in
    let any_residual equals residual_count > 0 in
    let lower equals schedule.claimed_aed - det_reductions in
    ReviewOutcome {
      -- mechanically_disposed_aed: 0.0
      -- deterministic_reductions_aed: det_reductions
      -- residual_discretion_lower_aed: 0.0
      -- residual_discretion_upper_aed: lower
      -- requires_human_judgment: any_residual
    }
```

## Test — facts of ENF 271/2025

```catala
#[test] declaration scope TestTaylor:
  review_scope scope IndemnityBasisReview
  output review content ReviewOutcome

scope TestTaylor:
  definition review_scope.schedule equals Schedule {
    -- claimed_aed: 128914.80
    -- objections: [
      Objection {
        -- objection: ClaimantDidWorkHimself
        -- names_specific_line_item: false
        -- factual_finding: Rejected_Unspecific
        -- named_amount_aed: 0.0
      };
      Objection {
        -- objection: DoubleCounselChargedForHearing
        -- names_specific_line_item: true
        -- factual_finding: Rejected_On_Evidence
        -- named_amount_aed: 0.0
      };
      Objection {
        -- objection: ExcessSeniorAssociateTime
        -- names_specific_line_item: false
        -- factual_finding: Requires_Human_Judgment
        -- named_amount_aed: 0.0
      }
    ]
  }

  definition review equals review_scope.review

  ## Mechanically: all objections either disposed or held to zero.
  ## Residual: the "excess senior associate time" category — predicate
  ## flags it; cannot resolve it. Human reviewer makes the call,
  ## producing the AED 8,914.80 deduction (claim 128,914.80 → 120,000).
  assertion review.deterministic_reductions_aed = 0.0
  assertion review.requires_human_judgment = true
```
